<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battenberg family</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as House of Battenberg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battenberg family was a morganatic branch of the grand ducal house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, founded when Prince Alexander of Hesse married Countess Julia Hauke, who was created Princess of Battenberg in 1858. Their sons included Alexander, the first prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, and Louis, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-sea-lord">First Sea Lord</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a>. In 1917 the British members renamed themselves Mountbatten.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battenberg-family.jpg" alt="Battenberg family" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NoahHK · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_Battenberg-Mountbatten.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
